# The subject's own array_bag.cpp allocates with `new int[...]` and frees with
# plain `delete` in three places (the destructor, insert() and clear()). That
# is a real defect, but it lives in a provided file: the grader compiles its
# own copy of array_bag.cpp, and none of the six graded files can reach it.
#
# These suppressions are scoped to frames inside array_bag, so the same mistake
# made anywhere in the graded code is still reported.
{
   provided array_bag frees a new[] block with plain delete
   Memcheck:Free
   fun:_ZdlPv
   fun:_ZN9array_bag*
}
{
   provided array_bag frees a new[] block with sized delete
   Memcheck:Free
   fun:_ZdlPvm
   fun:_ZN9array_bag*
}
